{"t":"m","f":3,"sv":24,"w":"df51ad18-b837-473b-accd-4c08a30ce777","al":"s"}
{"t":"n","a":1,"i":"f816444a-b012-4a5d-80ef-e29139284580","k":"module","n":"Mautrix Bridges Module","d":"NixOS module at `modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix` exposing `serv.mautrixBridges`, deployed on omegaServ. It runs the WhatsApp and Discord puppeting bridges against the `serv.continuwuity` homeserver, replacing the `dock.mau.dev/mautrix/*` containers from the host's previous Arch install. Slack is deliberately out of scope.\n\nIt wraps the upstream `services.mautrix-whatsapp` and `services.mautrix-discord` modules. Both ship homeserver defaults for `matrix-synapse` and `matrix-conduit` but none for `matrix-continuwuity`, so `homeserver.domain` and `homeserver.address` are set explicitly from the continuwuity options rather than inherited.\n\n`registerToSynapse` defaults to `services.matrix-synapse.enable`, which is false on this host, so neither bridge tries to write into a Synapse config that does not exist. That default is relied on rather than restated.\n\nRegistration is the part that has no declarative answer. Conduwuit-lineage homeservers carry no appservice options at all — unlike Synapse's `app_service_config_files`, they register appservices at runtime through the admin room. Each bridge's systemd preStart generates a registration YAML in its own state directory on first start; an operator then feeds that file to continuwuity once, by hand, in the admin room. The module cannot close that loop and does not pretend to.\n\nDatabases are PostgreSQL rather than the upstream SQLite default, because the surviving bridge state — including the WhatsApp pairing that would otherwise need the phone again — lives in the Postgres the old `mautrix_db` container ran out of /srv/mautrix/db. Each bridge gets its own database owned by its own system user, reached over the unix socket with peer authentication, so no password lands in the store. Restoring the old data into those databases is an operator step, not something this module performs.\n\nPorts carry over from the retired containers: 29318 for WhatsApp, 29334 for Discord, both loopback-only — the bridges are reached by the homeserver on the same host, never from outside, so nothing is opened in the firewall.\n\nOptions: `enable`, `whatsapp.enable`, `discord.enable`.","r":1214,"tg":["source:composite-make"]}
{"t":"n","a":2,"i":"5ee909af-f5dd-480b-b186-1dc441e5cf5c","k":"module","n":"Nextcloud AIO Mastercontainer Module","d":"NixOS module at `modules/nixos/serv/nextcloud-aio.nix` exposing `serv.nextcloudAio`, deployed on omegaServ. It declares the Nextcloud All-in-One mastercontainer in the flake and fronts it with Caddy, adopting the existing instance whose data already lives in `/home/docker/volumes`.\n\nDeliberately NOT a port to `services.nextcloud`. That module only ships Nextcloud 32 and 33, while this instance is on 30.0.17 and Nextcloud forbids skipping majors — and nixpkgs drops old majors every release, so the same stranding would recur. AIO walks majors sequentially by itself, and bundles Collabora, Talk, Imaginary, Fulltextsearch and Whiteboard, all of which this instance has enabled and none of which `services.nextcloud` provides. Docker therefore stays on this host deliberately, for exactly one workload.\n\nThe declarative boundary is one container. AIO's mastercontainer spawns and manages its ten siblings over the Docker socket, so the flake can declare only the mastercontainer; the rest are AIO's to own.\n\nSettings read off the running instance rather than chosen: domain cloud.benmac.xyz, apache_port 11000, timezone America/New_York, and no custom NEXTCLOUD_DATADIR, so the default 33G `nextcloud_aio_nextcloud_data` volume stands.\n\nThe one deliberate change from the old deployment is ingress. The old container set `apache_ip_binding = 0.0.0.0` and port 11000 was never opened in the firewall, so traffic almost certainly arrived over a Cloudflare Tunnel. This replaces that with the same path ntfy and continuwuity already use on this host: `APACHE_IP_BINDING=127.0.0.1`, and a Caddy virtual host for the domain reverse-proxying to 127.0.0.1:11000 over TLS-ALPN-01, since port 80 is not forwarded here. Cloudflared is retired.\n\nOptions: `enable`, `domain`, `acmeEmail`, `apachePort`, `adminPort` (the AIO admin UI, reachable on the LAN as it was before), and `timeZone`.\n\nFirewall: 443 for Caddy, the admin port on the LAN, and 3478 on **both TCP and UDP** for Talk's TURN server — the old host opened only TCP 3478, which would have left Talk's media relay broken from outside.","r":1214,"tg":["source:composite-make"]}
{"t":"n","a":3,"i":"04162eea-3a17-4c34-9921-5231f3685bca","k":"module","n":"NixOS Configuration Flake","d":"Defines a Nix flake that aggregates a set of inputs (Nixpkgs pins, Home Manager, external tools, and custom overlays) and provides an `outputs` function which builds NixOS system configurations for several hosts (matrixServ, nixWorks, omegaServ, phantomServ) as well as Home Manager user configurations for those hosts. It also declares package overlay functions for unfree and unstable packages, exposing them through the flake's `pkgs` attribute.","p":".","tg":["evidence:source","lang:nix","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":4,"i":"6fc31356-574f-4d9e-ab29-64ce9fbe3daa","k":"module","n":"Claude Settings","d":"Provides the configuration for the Claude code assistant, including lists of enabled and disabled MCP‑JSON servers, lifecycle event hooks that run at configurable points (such as tool use, session start/end, and message display), and the permissions governing which tools Claude may invoke. These settings allow users to tailor Claude’s runtime behavior and security posture via the .claude/settings.json and .claude/settings.local.json files.","p":".claude","tg":["layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":5,"i":"d1376d35-ce4c-4ed9-9e16-58809da14f03","k":"config_entry","n":"permissions","d":"Tool usage permissions configuration. See https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions and https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings#permission-settings See https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference for full list of tools available to Claude.","p":".claude/settings.json","r":6,"sp":[2,11,0,0],"tg":["arch:auto-attached","configkey:permissions","description:schema","layer:config","schema:schemastore/claude-code-settings","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":6,"i":"3a5af84f-1b35-4786-883e-b1ae2783f5f3","k":"file","n":"settings.json","d":"Provides the global Claude Code configuration, exposing the top‑level ‘hooks’ and ‘permissions’ entries that control lifecycle event hooks and tool‑usage permissions for the rest of the system.","p":".claude/settings.json","r":4,"tg":["layer:config","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":7,"i":"861344c5-6fbb-4ee5-8538-18f63d379e25","k":"config_entry","n":"disabledMcpjsonServers","d":"Takes a JSON array of strings representing server identifiers to disable. Stores this array under the key 'disabledMcpjsonServers' in the configuration file. Returns the stored array. Raises TypeError if the input is not an array of strings. Stores an empty list when given an empty array.","p":".claude/settings.local.json","r":10,"sp":[57,57,0,0],"tg":["arch:auto-attached","configkey:disabledMcpjsonServers","description:agent","layer:config","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":8,"i":"509199a4-3da1-4b5c-9698-5ccc62e9fe33","k":"config_entry","n":"enabledMcpjsonServers","d":"Takes no arguments and returns the value of the \"enabledMcpjsonServers\" key from the configuration file as a list of strings. If the key is missing or not an array, returns an empty list.","p":".claude/settings.local.json","r":10,"sp":[54,56,0,0],"tg":["arch:auto-attached","configkey:enabledMcpjsonServers","description:agent","layer:config","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":9,"i":"89bfea39-c072-4b67-9c19-2bbeb3d9fd4b","k":"config_entry","n":"permissions","d":"Provides a configuration entry named \"permissions\" that contains an \"allow\" field. The entry takes no parameters and returns a mapping with a single key \"allow\" whose value is a list of permission strings exactly as listed in the source. If the entry is missing, the configuration system should treat it as undefined (no default list).","p":".claude/settings.local.json","r":10,"sp":[2,53,0,0],"tg":["arch:auto-attached","configkey:permissions","description:agent","layer:config","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":10,"i":"a92ea44c-cf13-4824-88c1-6abd2b9c5fc8","k":"file","n":"settings.local.json","d":"Configuration for the Claude module's local settings, specifying which MCPJSON servers are enabled or disabled and defining permission rules.","p":".claude/settings.local.json","r":4,"tg":["layer:config","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":11,"i":"54c7ef5f-5261-491b-b031-7058fbe3d179","k":"config_entry","n":"mcpServers","d":"Expects a JSON object mapping server identifiers to their configuration objects. The object may be empty, meaning no MCP servers are configured. No other keys are required; any string key is accepted, and each value must be a JSON object representing that server's settings. The entry does not produce a return value; it solely defines configuration data. Validation consists only of confirming the top‑level value is an object.","p":".mcp.json","r":12,"sp":[2,2,0,0],"tg":["arch:auto-attached","configkey:mcpServers","description:agent","layer:config","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":12,"i":"3ce9c905-ba2d-4f2e-bfa2-a5c53ea53d70","k":"file","n":".mcp.json","d":"Configuration source defining the list of MCP server endpoints for the application.","p":".mcp.json","r":3,"tg":["layer:config","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":13,"i":"ff7fbcc7-61ae-4753-a5d2-9ed1a66541a4","k":"module","n":"confs","d":"A Python module named \"confs\" that supplies static HTML components for the start page and a Pomodoro bridge HTTP handler. It contains two files:\n- confs/startpage/index.html, which defines a collection of HTML component classes (e.g., #cal-add-btn, #cal-add-form, #cal-body, #chapter, #date, #focus, #gh-section, #link-list, #pomo-bar, #pomo-status, #pomo-track, #settings-bg, #settings-panel, #settings-trigger, #srv-list, #todo-add-btn, #todo-body, #todo-input-wrap) that each take no parameters and return or render the described HTML markup.\n- confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py, which defines:\n  * class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler): a BaseHTTPRequestHandler subclass that serves HTTP endpoints for a Pomodoro bridge.\n  * function _stream(): takes no arguments.\n  * function ping_host(host): takes a host string and performs an ICMP ping with TCP‑connect fallback.\nThe module’s purpose is to provide reusable UI fragments for the start page and a lightweight HTTP bridge for Pomodoro functionality. Primary symbols a caller is expected to use are the Handler class for serving the bridge, the ping_host function for connectivity checks, and the HTML component classes such as #settings-panel or #pomo-bar for embedding UI elements.","p":"confs","r":3,"tg":["arch:empty","description:agent","layer:architecture","provisional:structure","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":14,"i":"48dd4a03-cd90-4606-a247-8abbbb7af425","k":"module","n":"Start Page Dashboard","d":"Provides a customizable HTML start page that displays a Pomodoro timer bar, settings panel, to‑do list, calendar and server status, backed by a lightweight Python HTTP bridge (pomo‑bridge.py) which streams Pomodoro module output and offers ICMP/TCP host ping checks to the page via a local web server.","p":"confs/startpage","r":13,"tg":["evidence:source","lang:html","lang:python","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":15,"i":"4c1b3055-d2cf-4b30-a2d1-a4258ff0625c","k":"class","n":"#cal-add-btn","d":"Takes no parameters. Returns a static HTML string: a <div> with class=\"cal-label\" containing the text \"schedule \" followed by a <button> element with id=\"cal-add-btn\", title=\"add event (a)\" and inner text \"+\". The output is exactly the fragment '<div class=\"cal-label\">schedule <button id=\"cal-add-btn\" title=\"add event (a)\">+</button></div>'. No errors are raised and the result is deterministic.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[495,495,37,94],"sh":"cc2c59b3a39f126e4e7e76863f2538390ac48e39f729502bea441d1cc203ea83","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":16,"i":"661a593e-645c-4e2f-879d-22449a84e754","k":"class","n":"#cal-add-form","d":"Takes no parameters and returns an HTML string containing a <div> with id=\"cal-add-form\". Inside the div are two input elements: a required <input> with id=\"cal-add-time\" and type=\"time\", and a <input> with id=\"cal-add-title\", type=\"text\", and placeholder=\"event name\". The returned HTML is exactly as shown, with no additional wrapper or surrounding content. No error conditions are defined.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[496,499,5,11],"sh":"142c2e4eb542c6b5da655d8d2bad298f6d70bffa4a8bd42366cd34a820720eda","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":17,"i":"4af14afa-dcc7-4a9c-82f9-476288162d23","k":"class","n":"#cal-add-time","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":16,"sp":[497,498,7,7],"tg":["lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":18,"i":"52b1cf7d-6840-4fec-a530-d163a65a9212","k":"class","n":"#cal-add-title","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":16,"sp":[498,499,7,5],"tg":["lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":19,"i":"86167994-6bd2-4d03-8b53-9b8ef7accc66","k":"class","n":"#cal-body","d":"Takes no parameters and returns the literal HTML string \"<div id=\\\"cal-body\\\"></div>\" representing a div element with id \"cal-body\".","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[500,500,5,30],"sh":"3a59ab43567a649611d601a6e9bbf67d71a8601f85ed0a0cf6ab377619321e7a","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":20,"i":"9237b506-8af9-4f03-9c8d-e03c05b1b02a","k":"class","n":"#chapter","d":"Produces a static HTML element: an empty <span> tag with id=\"chapter\" and no inner content or additional attributes. Takes no parameters and returns no value; its effect is the presence of this element in the rendered page.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[484,484,7,33],"sh":"e5f1629a31e9d12ec0d63112c49cd05a5a888ce041064cd620430a3a522958dc","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":21,"i":"0f47589a-16fd-4739-ac02-20ccde01b3d5","k":"class","n":"#date","d":"Takes no parameters. Returns the HTML string \"<span id=\\\"date\\\"></span>\" which renders a span element with id=\"date\" and no inner content.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[483,483,7,30],"sh":"62ee8e7bbbbe4c53137266a96c8427fd8f0863112b4c78907bfe4f3e34fdc202","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":22,"i":"3fa3f719-54ca-4d28-8e9d-a0b3d09afd2b","k":"class","n":"#focus","d":"Takes no parameters. Returns an empty HTML <div> element with id=\"focus\", contenteditable=\"true\", data‑placeholder=\"what's the focus?\" and spellcheck=\"false\". When rendered the element is editable, shows the placeholder text while empty, and does not perform spellchecking.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[488,491,5,32],"sh":"046c45cb6436b4090b8e69573d2b7cc431cafcbd59a287df5c1c3ae36bb32a53","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":23,"i":"e2b284d8-dd27-4fe2-afaa-a413dc5e8499","k":"class","n":"#gh-body","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":24,"sp":[523,523,7,31],"tg":["lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":24,"i":"1f2841d0-fba1-46f6-b19e-0cfe1cd75b98","k":"class","n":"#gh-section","d":"Renders a static HTML fragment consisting of a <div> with id=\"gh-section\" and style=\"display:none\". Inside it contains a <div class=\"section-label\" style=\"color:var(--yellow)\">github</div> and an empty <div id=\"gh-body\"></div>. Takes no parameters and produces no return value; the function's effect is to output this exact markup when invoked.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[521,524,5,11],"sh":"008b098fd32bce5a413afceff846b552dbff450993a9a2bef70b0f53e9e7f055","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":25,"i":"0cad0771-b1ad-40ad-9946-e96e83b82f45","k":"class","n":"#link-list","d":"Takes no arguments and returns an HTML <div> element with class \"link-list\" and id \"link-list\". No side effects.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[518,518,7,51],"sh":"babce30bd87ad32395c114bf553a3bb7b035c9ded5b7c23063f851389f3deea7","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":26,"i":"76617a20-cc13-4cff-aac4-883da36829fe","k":"class","n":"#pomo-bar","d":"Produces a static HTML `<div>` element with id \"pomo-bar\", an onclick attribute that calls `pomoAction('toggle')`, and a title attribute \"click to toggle\". Takes no inputs and returns the exact HTML markup string `<div id=\"pomo-bar\" onclick=\"pomoAction('toggle')\" title=\"click to toggle\"></div>`; no errors or variations are possible.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[412,412,1,81],"sh":"9c71738274f1736d06a832e83fb6daeeddee0f51df79720660b54aaeefa3ba11","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":27,"i":"7fc1c676-3b09-452c-bbb5-0e8374a66db6","k":"class","n":"#pomo-status","d":"Produces a static HTML fragment containing a `div` element with id=\"pomo-status\", class=\"pomo-status\", and an onclick handler that calls `pomoAction('toggle')`. The element’s content is the Japanese text \"ポモ\". Takes no parameters and always returns exactly this markup as a string. No side effects or external resources are used.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[526,528,5,11],"sh":"29d37ab98fdcd44c8b54098d2e747d712fa12f9c71d6989b17dc00713cb1c2c6","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":28,"i":"7581673b-21a0-4655-9404-80a5970576e7","k":"class","n":"#pomo-track","d":"Takes no parameters and returns the literal HTML string \"<div id=\\\"pomo-track\\\"></div>\".","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[411,411,1,28],"sh":"7ccd974e72d7f21e680302269e87f64f06ac7ced207700393a0dcfa7c0e668ae","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
