{"t":"n","a":42,"i":"72a40c5c-354d-42fc-a3a0-0436713f3ffe","k":"class","n":"#settings-bg","d":"Takes no parameters. Returns an HTML string representing an empty <div> element with id=\"settings-bg\" and an onclick attribute set to \"closeSettings()\".","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[415,415,1,55],"sh":"0610cc2c5d4527115bc8773e431a8321e4855f0dd757ddfeec8468746a69c858","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":43,"i":"e3982bc6-4c07-4c18-9e5c-76be181c5b3d","k":"class","n":"#settings-panel","d":"The node renders a static settings panel UI and takes no arguments. It returns the exact HTML markup shown in the source—a <div id=\"settings-panel\"> containing a header with a title and reset/close buttons, a scrollable area with sections for Nextcloud (enable toggle, URL, username, app password, calendar fields), Pomodoro (work minutes, short‑break minutes, long‑break minutes, cycles per long break), a server list area with an add‑server button, and a GitHub personal‑access‑token field with a hint. The return value is a string of HTML (or a DOM element) that can be inserted into the document. No errors are raised and the output is deterministic.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[417,476,1,7],"sh":"2333a9d351048dd43667c4721c340e16ab2bf1926d2918f354aa9d6e835eae72","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":44,"i":"c9f5548e-0088-4522-8fdb-70be44f7e00d","k":"class","n":"#settings-trigger","d":"Renders a <button> element with id \"settings-trigger\", title \"Settings (,)\", onclick attribute \"openSettings()\", and inner text \"⚙\".","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[414,414,1,89],"sh":"6f7f8fd700e16457037ef479d4e582df432f6fcf8fd3575c7e01f3abf03c0a9d","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":45,"i":"96552979-9247-418e-83a4-2c2be0de3808","k":"class","n":"#srv-list","d":"Takes no parameters and returns the HTML string <div class=\"srv-list\" id=\"srv-list\"></div> representing an empty container with class \"srv-list\" and id \"srv-list\".","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[515,515,7,49],"sh":"2ee3547c0eba47d9cfd0d3cf7975190d8a9928c90be4f415aa472100ae403578","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":46,"i":"eff13156-ef8a-4eb3-9352-9e18d2ef1b1b","k":"class","n":"#todo-add-btn","d":"Renders a div with class \"todo-label\" containing the text \"todo \" and a button element with id \"todo-add-btn\", title \"add todo (t)\", and inner text \"+\". Takes no inputs and returns the HTML string representing this markup.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[504,504,34,91],"sh":"76856957dd2d180a6c8f49d1fd679d2863465b69ca55e5f3ff7413799d609ae2","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":47,"i":"44067b5b-195c-4de5-bf3b-65332cb18363","k":"class","n":"#todo-body","d":"Takes no parameters. Returns an HTML fragment that consists exactly of a <div> element with id=\"todo-body\" and no inner content.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[508,508,5,31],"sh":"d2e8bbaf4d7cad5b6a0283866bcc820b74de519dbe91cdc57da76d389725b2f4","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":48,"i":"6b4fdb73-4bf2-40ee-8287-aea3fd3a0533","k":"class","n":"#todo-input","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":49,"sp":[506,507,7,5],"tg":["lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":49,"i":"42546bbe-4ef4-4166-af05-fd6749ed9947","k":"class","n":"#todo-input-wrap","d":"Takes no parameters. Returns a string containing the exact HTML markup `<div id=\"todo-input-wrap\"><input id=\"todo-input\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"what needs doing?\"></div>`. The markup always includes a div with id \"todo-input-wrap\" wrapping an input element with id \"todo-input\", type \"text\", and placeholder \"what needs doing?\". No errors are raised and the output is deterministic.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":50,"sp":[505,507,5,11],"sh":"d31defbe89911369b8b31e1d5fca7ac171165f1bc238828cd8918a5e07c26583","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:html","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":50,"i":"483c7a0e-90b0-41f9-87c3-73fe6aad0928","k":"file","n":"index.html","d":"HTML template for the application’s landing page, served at the root URL as the default start page.","p":"confs/startpage/index.html","r":14,"tg":["lang:html","source:tree-sitter","stub:unsupported-language"]}
{"t":"n","a":51,"i":"5344cb06-cf11-423e-b5b7-bd74ee276892","k":"class","n":"Handler","d":"Handler is a BaseHTTPRequestHandler subclass that serves HTTP endpoints for a Pomodoro bridge. It requires no constructor arguments; the server passes the request. For any OPTIONS request it responds with status 204 and adds Access-Control-Allow-Origin \"*\" and Access-Control-Allow-Methods \"GET, POST, OPTIONS\" headers. For GET requests: if the path is \"/state\", it acquires the global _lock, JSON‑encodes the global _state dictionary, and returns status 200 with Content-Type \"application/json\" and the same CORS headers; if the path is \"/ping\", it reads the query parameter \"host\", returning status 400 with only the CORS headers when missing or empty, otherwise calling ping_host(host), JSON‑encodes the result, and returns status 200 with Content-Type \"application/json\" and the CORS headers; for any other path it returns status 404 with the CORS headers. For POST requests: if the path is \"/toggle\" or \"/reset\", it runs the external command defined by the global constant POMO with argument \"toggle\" or \"reset\" respectively, discarding output, then returns status 200 with the CORS headers; otherwise it returns status 404 with the CORS headers. All responses include the CORS headers. The handler suppresses logging by overriding log_message to do nothing.","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":52,"sg":"class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):","sp":[68,119,1,13],"sh":"d461741e0ed4d021a60c900ea52fde315e0bfcee330750abaad24c8da1ab3fdc","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":52,"i":"3e3ea943-4259-4aaf-9e88-54b730851a11","k":"file","n":"pomo-bridge.py","d":"Provides a lightweight HTTP server that bridges the pomodoro Waybar module (default executable \"waybar-module-pomodoro\") to external consumers, listening on port 9421 and handling requests with the Handler class; also offers a ping_host utility for host reachability checks.","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":14,"tg":["lang:python","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":53,"i":"a48f3ebd-4970-43fb-a6f8-35bc1137aff0","k":"function","n":"_stream","d":"Takes no arguments. Continuously launches the POMO command as a subprocess, reads its stdout line‑by‑line, decodes each line as UTF‑8, strips whitespace, skips empty lines, parses each non‑empty line as JSON, and merges the resulting dictionary into the global _state while holding the global _lock; lines that cannot be parsed as JSON are ignored. If the subprocess exits or any exception is raised while spawning or reading, the function sleeps for two seconds then restarts the subprocess. The function runs indefinitely and never returns (returns None only if the thread is terminated).","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":52,"sg":"def _stream():","sp":[13,31,1,26],"sh":"f332aeb969b68f98b6dca1aa2efc9a6266a4a275218ee86344dd00e9a731d3e4","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:private"]}
{"t":"n","a":54,"i":"121dc060-9a55-459a-8683-48aee7803e3f","k":"function","n":"ping_host","d":"ICMP ping with TCP-connect fallback. Returns {up, latency}.","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":52,"sg":"def ping_host(host):","lt":"[\"ping\",\"-c\",\"-W\",\"time=(d+.?d*)\",\"up\",\"latency\"]","sp":[37,65,1,39],"sh":"a52a7ff9f2efdba8bc909ec8b3f167adcdcda988e5e5914daf58ef30716dd254","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:docstring","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":55,"i":"0a2637ba-3643-4890-8e0d-efe79498b594","k":"method","n":"_cors","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":51,"sg":"def _cors(self):","lt":"[\"Access-Control-Allow-Origin\",\"Access-Control-Allow-Methods\",\"GET, POST, OPTIONS\"]","sp":[69,71,5,79],"tg":["lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:private"]}
{"t":"n","a":56,"i":"d4af114a-7818-465e-9ca1-d00694dd2a2f","k":"method","n":"do_GET","d":"Handles a GET request on the HTTP handler instance (self). Parses self.path with urlparse; if the path is \"/state\" it acquires the global _lock, serializes the global _state to JSON bytes, sends HTTP 200 with Content‑Type \"application/json\" and CORS headers via self._cors(), then writes the body. If the path is \"/ping\" it extracts the query parameter \"host\" (first value, stripped); if the host string is empty it sends HTTP 400 with CORS headers and no body. Otherwise it calls ping_host(host), JSON‑encodes the returned value, sends HTTP 200 with Content‑Type \"application/json\" and CORS headers, then writes the body. For any other path it sends HTTP 404 with CORS headers and no body. The method returns None.","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":51,"sg":"def do_GET(self):","lt":"[\"/state\",\"Content-Type\",\"application/json\",\"/ping\",\"host\"]","sp":[78,105,5,31],"sh":"ae8fbf0075a0851e81c232f7c1fc95a2611eda62946b9783e785dd8c355fcb7b","tg":["description:agent","evidence:source","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":57,"i":"f1e81d5e-5264-46b1-ac01-06ddbce373a6","k":"method","n":"do_OPTIONS","d":"Sends a 204 No Content response, invokes the internal _cors method to add CORS headers, and finalizes the HTTP headers with end_headers.","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":51,"sg":"def do_OPTIONS(self):","sp":[73,76,5,27],"sh":"bcb7be2f35c002beda989dc4479b88d8c0f148c7c273e59f920d16e8c2bb6cf1","tg":["description:agent","evidence:source","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":58,"i":"74674c86-9b29-4e8f-b477-06cd768dbdef","k":"method","n":"do_POST","d":"Handles a POST request by mapping the request path to a command using the fixed dictionary {\"/toggle\": \"toggle\", \"/reset\": \"reset\"}; if the path is found, runs subprocess.run([POMO, arg], capture_output=True) and sends an HTTP 200 response, otherwise sends an HTTP 404 response; then calls self._cors() to add CORS headers and finishes the response with end_headers().","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":51,"sg":"def do_POST(self):","lt":"[\"/toggle\",\"toggle\",\"/reset\",\"reset\"]","sp":[107,116,5,27],"sh":"c084a5187d4683bba09de01ee774c6948d01afaed31b48e6c1df41dd869512ab","tg":["description:agent","evidence:source","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":59,"i":"b176ddbd-cd2f-4a0d-9c5b-3543a9a100a2","k":"method","n":"log_message","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":51,"sg":"def log_message(self, *_):","sp":[118,119,5,13],"tg":["lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":60,"i":"16f72a2a-ede0-44c2-862d-351bebee42de","k":"variable","n":"POMO","d":"POMO = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"waybar-module-pomodoro\"","p":"confs/startpage/pomo-bridge.py","r":52,"sp":[6,6,1,70],"sh":"538200d7040f51c915af4f1a076fb4c354e7694f59fcd933b66c831448b94ef1","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
