{"t":"n","a":98,"i":"e6e291da-bfd0-4d81-8229-ad2b61faaeac","k":"external","n":"subprocess","d":"Runs an external command specified by a command string or sequence of arguments, optionally with shell execution, environment variables, working directory, input data, timeout, and output capture. Returns a Result object containing the original arguments, exit status code, and captured standard output and error streams. If the optional flag check is true and the command exits with a non‑zero status, raises a ProcessError; otherwise the Result is returned. Raises FileNotFoundError if the command cannot be located. The function passes through any provided environment variables and working directory, and uses the default system locale and character encoding unless overridden. No other side effects beyond executing the command are performed.","p":"external:subprocess","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":99,"i":"c4276105-2a98-4675-a7ac-b042cd2965ad","k":"external","n":"sys","d":"External module 'sys' from the Python standard library. Provides interpreter state and functions (e.g., argv, exit, modules, path, version). Takes no parameters, returns a module object exposing its attributes. No errors are raised by the module itself; attribute access may raise AttributeError if the attribute does not exist.","p":"external:sys","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":100,"i":"caaeacf2-5351-4aa3-828d-157427eb2fb4","k":"external","n":"tempfile","d":"Provides the standard library \"tempfile\" module, exposing functions to create, manage, and delete temporary files and directories such as mkstemp, TemporaryFile, mkdtemp, and related context‑managed helpers.","p":"external:tempfile","lt":"[]","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":101,"i":"d05f3dd9-e7ba-41ee-8b15-27dc3d5ff656","k":"external","n":"threading","d":"Provides the Python standard library threading module, exposing Thread, Lock, RLock, Event, Condition, Semaphore, BoundedSemaphore, Timer, Barrier, local classes and the functions start_new_thread, current_thread, enumerate, active_count, and get_ident. The module does not take any input parameters and its members behave as defined by Python's threading package.","p":"external:threading","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":102,"i":"3cf0a6d5-a688-4a4b-9b26-fc20373fbd1b","k":"external","n":"time","d":"Provides utilities for working with dates and times, including the Time and Duration types. Exposes functions such as Now() to obtain the current instant, Parse(layout, value) to parse a string, Format(layout) to format a Time, Add(d Duration) to add a duration, Sub(other Time) to compute elapsed duration, Unix() to get the Unix timestamp, and constants for unit durations such as Nanosecond, Millisecond, etc. All time values are absolute instants relative to the Unix epoch.","p":"external:time","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":103,"i":"e120fd8e-66d2-4f41-bd02-234212b6e861","k":"external","n":"tomllib","d":"The tomllib module provides utilities to parse TOML data. It exposes two callables: `load(f: BinaryIO) -> dict`, which reads TOML from a binary file‑like object and returns a Python dictionary representing the document; and `loads(s: str) -> dict`, which parses a TOML‑formatted string and returns a dictionary. Both raise `tomllib.TOMLDecodeError` on malformed input. The module does not perform any I/O beyond reading the provided object and does not modify the input data.","p":"external:tomllib","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":104,"i":"e049a2d8-8ba0-4490-8089-c5be8caf696b","k":"external","n":"types","d":"Exports shared type definitions for the NixOS project. It does not accept any inputs nor produce runtime values; its purpose is to provide type information used by other symbols in the codebase.","p":"external:types","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":105,"i":"32c2f763-242e-45c2-9592-cb59258f2e3a","k":"external","n":"unittest","d":"Provides the standard library unittest module; takes no parameters, performs no actions, and offers classes and functions for defining and running tests as defined by the Python unittest package.","p":"external:unittest","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":106,"i":"2ab59f6b-c526-45e8-aeeb-0ca93f55c355","k":"external","n":"urllib","d":"Represents the Python standard library urllib package; takes no arguments and provides no direct return value. It exposes the submodules request, parse, error, and robotparser, each conforming to the interfaces defined by the Python standard library. This node is used for import resolution and does not perform runtime actions itself.","p":"external:urllib","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":107,"i":"81f6b80f-e758-4b58-8aeb-f957fe997f0b","k":"external","n":"waybar-pomodoro","d":"Provides the Waybar Pomodoro external module for the Waybar status bar. It is an external binary invoked by Waybar; takes no parameters from this codebase and does not return values to callers within this project.","p":"external:waybar-pomodoro","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":108,"i":"a742cd78-5c17-420a-b303-79bc69d4d96b","k":"external","n":"xremap-flake","d":"External reference to the Nix flake named \"xremap-flake\" in the \"nixos\" project.","p":"external:xremap-flake","tg":["description:agent","layer:dependency","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":109,"i":"b8e514f7-3385-4ddf-b513-a3664c969d5b","k":"file","n":"flake.nix","d":"Provides the Nix flake that declares the NixOS configuration's inputs (multiple nixpkgs channels and home-manager) and supplies the outputs attribute set used to build the system.","p":"flake.nix","r":3,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":110,"i":"893d9993-c6c0-4b79-9298-5e215902ca1d","k":"function","n":"outputs","d":"Takes an attribute set `inputs` that must contain the keys `self`, `nixpkgs`, `home-manager`, `nixpkgs-master`, `nixpkgs-unstable`, and may contain additional attributes. It returns an attribute set with two top‑level keys, `nixosConfigurations` and `homeConfigurations`. Under `nixosConfigurations` it provides NixOS system definitions for the hosts `nixWorks`, `phantomServ`, `omegaServ`, and `matrixServ`, each built with `nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem` using `system = \"x86_64-linux\"`, `specialArgs = { inherit inputs; }`, and a module list that (a) sets `nixpkgs.config` to a configuration containing `permittedInsecurePackages = [ \"electron-39.8.10\" \"olm-3.2.16\" ];`, (b) adds the overlays `overlay-unfree`, `overlay-master`, `overlay-master-unfree`, `overlay-unstable`, `overlay-unstable-unfree`, and a custom overlay defining `waybar-pomodoro` via `callPackage ./pkgs/waybar-module-pomodoro.nix { inherit inputs; }`, and (c) includes the host‑specific NixOS configuration file (`./hosts/.../configuration.nix`). Under `homeConfigurations` it provides Home Manager configurations for the same hosts, each built with `home-manager.lib.homeManagerConfiguration` using `extraSpecialArgs = { inherit inputs; osConfig = nixosConfigurations.<host>.config; flakeAttr = \"<host>\"; }`, `inherit pkgs`, and a module list that mirrors the NixOS module list (setting `nixpkgs.config`, adding the same overlays, and the custom `waybar-pomodoro` overlay) plus the host‑specific Home Manager module file (`./hosts/.../home.nix`). If any required key is missing from `inputs`, evaluation fails with a Nix attribute‑missing error. The function does not perform any I/O; it is pure and deterministic for a given `inputs` set.","p":"flake.nix","r":109,"sg":"outputs = { self, nixpkgs, home-manager, nixpkgs-master, nixpkgs-unstable, ... }@inputs:","lt":"[\"x86_64-linux\",\"electron-39.8.10\",\"olm-3.2.16\",\"nixWorks\",\"phantomServ\",\"omegaServ\"]","sp":[59,231,3,7],"sh":"43024343fdb609172f9a46d742521b0b7c7ebc0ae0c0c2908b6319fffc119fd9","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:agent","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
