{"t":"n","a":146,"i":"6103fa6b-3449-43c0-891f-8c8a215de2bb","k":"subsystem","n":"hosts — NixOS Host Configurations","d":"NixOS host definition modules for each machine (matrixServ, nixBlade, omegaServ, phantomServ). Each module assembles the system configuration by importing shared NixOS modules and Home Manager modules, providing a complete declarative setup for the respective host.","p":"hosts","tg":["evidence:signatures","layer:overview","overview:rung:directory","source:overview-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":147,"i":"e4a05a6a-9466-4f3f-bcf4-a5b925d59c61","k":"module","n":"Matrix Server Host Configuration","d":"Provides the NixOS configuration for the matrixServ host, configuring Azure VM hardware, boot settings, networking, firewall, system packages, automatic upgrades, and enabling the Matrix service with encryption, Slack notifications, and backup settings.","p":"hosts/matrixServ","r":146,"tg":["evidence:source","lang:nix","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":148,"i":"ecdd7dda-af18-40c2-a1f8-70168566c1f6","k":"file","n":"configuration.nix","d":"NixOS host configuration for the matrixServ machine, assembling hardware configuration and shared server modules, and enabling the Matrix service with its domain, admin, encryption, and backup settings, plus system-wide options such as installed packages, firewall rules, swap, automatic Nix garbage collection, experimental Nix features, time zone, auto-upgrade, and root SSH key management.","p":"hosts/matrixServ/configuration.nix","r":147,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
