{"t":"n","a":205,"i":"5b8a38e5-9738-46cf-80bf-ced2e3881cc1","k":"variable","n":"postVM","d":"postVM = ''\n  set -euo pipefail\n  current_size=$(stat -c '%s' \"$diskImage\")\n  remainder=$(( current_size % 1048576 ))\n  if [ \"$remainder\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    pad=0\n  else\n    pad=$(( 1048576 - remainder ))\n  fi\n  new_size=$(( current_size + pad ))\n  ${pkgs.qemu-utils}/bin/qemu-img resize -f raw \"$diskImage\" \"$new_size\"\n  ${pkgs.qemu-utils}/bin/qemu-img convert -f raw -o subformat=fixed,force_size -O vpc \"$diskImage\" \"$out/disk.vhd\"\n  rm \"$diskImage\"\n'';","p":"hosts/matrixServ/hardware-configuration.nix","r":206,"sp":[46,59,5,8],"sh":"5ed2fbb77ecbabbb04cd50cd0532cd071617d590e84e919813b6ecdeef490bee","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":206,"i":"f4090259-619a-47b7-8c98-638d5a52197f","k":"variable","n":"system.build.azureImage","d":"system.build.azureImage = import (modulesPath + \"/../lib/make-disk-image.nix\") {\n  inherit config lib pkgs;\n  name = \"azure-image\";\n  partitionTableType = \"efi\";\n  format = \"raw\";\n  postVM = ''\n    set -euo pipefail\n    current_size=$(stat -c '%s' \"$diskImage\")\n    remainder=$(( current_size % 1048576 ))\n    if [ \"$remainder\" -eq 0 ]; then\n      pad=0\n    else\n      pad=$(( 1048576 - remainder ))\n    fi\n    new_size=$(( current_size + pad ))\n    ${pkgs.qemu-utils}/bin/qemu-img resize -f raw \"$diskImage\" \"$new_size\"\n… (truncated)","p":"hosts/matrixServ/hardware-configuration.nix","r":186,"sp":[41,60,3,5],"sh":"f03627ffbc76904d3cdc941f9d6319d12b740bcf324c50b20bf7a8cd0688ef15","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":207,"i":"49e8723e-be42-4dac-a588-59ea04f2b4bd","k":"module","n":"NixBlade Host Configuration","d":"Provides the complete NixOS configuration for the host named nixBlade. It combines the generated hardware configuration, custom systemd slice throttling for coding agents, coredump size limits, Nix store hygiene settings, remote build machine definitions, and a Home Manager user profile. The module configures system services (SSH, display manager, graphics, networking, power management), installs packages, sets environment variables, and enables various user‑level programs and features such as Tailscale, Mullvad VPN, and desktop environments.","p":"hosts/nixBlade","r":146,"tg":["evidence:source","lang:nix","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":208,"i":"43160dd2-3c8e-4f79-819c-316ba882726b","k":"file","n":"agent-throttle.nix","d":"Defines host-specific resource limits for agent workloads on the nixBlade machine: configures Nix parallelism, adjusts the nix-daemon's CPU/IO weight, creates an \"agents\" systemd slice with CPU, IO, and memory caps, adds a shell alias to launch the \"claude\" agent via systemd-run, and enables zram swap.","p":"hosts/nixBlade/agent-throttle.nix","r":207,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
