{"t":"n","a":339,"i":"8709b663-2bbb-44d8-b54f-4b2ab504e18f","k":"file","n":"remote-builds.nix","d":"Points this laptop's nix at the XiaServer build host over the tailnet. Sets nix.distributedBuilds and builders-use-substitutes, and declares one nix.buildMachines entry at the Tailscale IP 100.96.50.71 (user graphide-build, ssh-ng, maxJobs 3, speedFactor 4) — a tailnet address rather than the former LAN 10.0.0.35 so builds keep working away from home while still taking a direct LAN path when at home. Because nix-daemon opens the connection as root, it also pins the host's ed25519 key system-wide via programs.ssh.knownHosts across all three of its names, and sets ConnectTimeout 10 for that host in programs.ssh.extraConfig so an offline builder fails over to a local build in seconds instead of a TCP timeout. XiaServer is a node shared in from tail028f45.ts.net, so its bare MagicDNS short name does not resolve here.","p":"hosts/nixBlade/remote-builds.nix","r":207,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":340,"i":"71962f7f-341f-4392-88aa-1f76a91b144a","k":"variable","n":"hostName","d":"hostName = \"100.96.50.71\";","p":"hosts/nixBlade/remote-builds.nix","r":345,"sp":[139,139,7,33],"sh":"38fa57a2ef44ab254b92305f5e49641991e35bfaabafea1037c8b86f40d142c2","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","nix:leaf","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
