{"t":"n","a":468,"i":"563600cd-87e8-47e2-b0ef-0a9a0e21a992","k":"subsystem","n":"modules — System configuration collection","d":"Root collection of Nix modules used to configure the entire system, providing entry points for host-specific imports.","p":"modules","tg":["evidence:signatures","layer:overview","overview:rung:directory","source:overview-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":469,"i":"5a840688-4f58-47b0-83d8-61d6efdbaaaf","k":"module","n":"Home Manager Configuration","d":"Aggregates Home Manager sub-modules (desktop, term, rice) and defines options such as enabling media, setting a Gruvbox color scheme, configuring GTK and Qt themes, cursor settings, session environment variables, and Flatpak extensions, with most settings gated by the desktop.enable flag.","p":"modules/home-manager","r":470,"tg":["evidence:source","lang:nix","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":470,"i":"ca4c8b10-f834-4d67-a871-c11e4ad65550","k":"subsystem","n":"modules/home-manager — User‑level Home Manager configuration","d":"Nix Home Manager modules that define a user's environment, themes and base settings, imported by host configurations.","p":"modules/home-manager","r":468,"tg":["evidence:signatures","layer:overview","overview:rung:directory","source:overview-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":471,"i":"59ea3a2e-6625-4718-85ba-6ddc8635f30a","k":"file","n":"default.nix","d":"Aggregates Home Manager sub-modules (desktop, terminal, rice, and flatpak) and provides a media.enable option for enabling media support.","p":"modules/home-manager/default.nix","r":469,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":472,"i":"cfdc2f99-4c80-44f2-aa69-6e1a9f903ab6","k":"variable","n":"imports","d":"imports = [\n  ./desktop\n  ./term\n  ./rice.nix\n  inputs.nix-flatpak.homeManagerModules.nix-flatpak\n];","p":"modules/home-manager/default.nix","r":471,"sp":[3,8,3,5],"sh":"dce99c520623155d16a895a5e8d97c8817798275b0e33ec6416cdeed0512c7a9","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":473,"i":"9eb494e1-b8ef-41c4-80cc-a8711cd04188","k":"variable","n":"media","d":"media = {\n  enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable media\";\n};","p":"modules/home-manager/default.nix","r":474,"sp":[10,12,5,7],"sh":"6e580ae1ff64556bba41c99b97a5a157cbc8f584b6d74ab5892f6aceef719bd3","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":474,"i":"8f714daf-f7a7-4895-b2e9-d35e672a2a2f","k":"variable","n":"options","d":"options = {\n  media = {\n    enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable media\";\n  };\n};","p":"modules/home-manager/default.nix","r":471,"sp":[9,13,3,5],"sh":"e98b89b4965cdc6b39f2d7e435c736d2abd4167a4e9af439b514d0999f7e6a91","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":475,"i":"49c022e6-b4bd-4edb-944e-13f9341faf53","k":"module","n":"Desktop Home Manager Configuration","d":"Provides a Home Manager configuration for a desktop environment. It defines a top‑level `desktop.enable` option and imports a collection of sub‑modules (apps, env, gaming, Japanese input, communications, sync, office, media, health alerts). When enabled it installs a suite of desktop packages (e.g., thunderbird, fluffychat, element‑desktop, games via flatpak, media tools, office utilities) and configures related services such as flatpak package overrides, systemd user timers for health alerts, ZSH aliases, and KDE Connect. It also includes a Python utility (`asar.py`) that can rewrite ASAR archives in place, recomputing offsets, sizes, and integrity hashes, used by the Proton Mail and Signal theme‑patching modules.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop","r":476,"tg":["evidence:source","lang:nix","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":476,"i":"3221c88a-892d-4df9-a5b1-26bd28c71302","k":"subsystem","n":"modules/home-manager/desktop — Desktop environment configuration","d":"Nix modules configuring desktop applications and environment; primarily Nix with auxiliary Python scripts for tooling.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop","r":470,"tg":["evidence:signatures","layer:overview","overview:rung:directory","source:overview-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":477,"i":"fa14c83c-bd90-4ab2-b2bc-08a6f11d2a38","k":"file","n":"EE.nix","d":"Provides the home-manager desktop configuration for AI tools, exposing enable options and installing aichat and a custom getchips script when enabled.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/EE.nix","r":475,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":478,"i":"5871811a-57d6-435e-9d78-0e1af06175fb","k":"variable","n":"config","d":"config = lib.mkIf config.ai.enable {\n  home.packages = [\n    pkgs.aichat\n    (pkgs.writeShellApplication\n      {\n        name = \"getchips\";\n        runtimeInputs = [ pkgs.rofi pkgs.zathura];\n        text = ''\n          ls ~/Documents/Chips | rofi -dmenu | xargs -I {} zathura \"~/Documents/Chips/{}\"\n        '';\n      })\n    (lib.mkIf config.ai.localrun.enable pkgs.unfree.openai-whisper)\n    (lib.mkIf config.ai.localrun.enable pkgs.ollama)\n  ];\n};","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/EE.nix","r":477,"sp":[9,23,3,5],"sh":"2cae15673095f9434ed57fab0ae04433baef8ce261c1f314940b80f638a95062","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":479,"i":"b0dbdf1d-faaa-4f37-b1c9-aa9e4995597d","k":"variable","n":"engineer","d":"engineer = {\n  enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable AI\";\n  localrun.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable local AI\";\n};","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/EE.nix","r":481,"sp":[4,7,5,7],"sh":"0c96f6d12d9938c1398bba6c1ac1daf17e858f2b0245a4073901722bb894895f","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":480,"i":"47da48c9-9b2b-49bb-a674-605fadd508ab","k":"variable","n":"home.packages","d":"home.packages = [\n  pkgs.aichat\n  (pkgs.writeShellApplication\n    {\n      name = \"getchips\";\n      runtimeInputs = [ pkgs.rofi pkgs.zathura];\n      text = ''\n        ls ~/Documents/Chips | rofi -dmenu | xargs -I {} zathura \"~/Documents/Chips/{}\"\n      '';\n    })\n  (lib.mkIf config.ai.localrun.enable pkgs.unfree.openai-whisper)\n  (lib.mkIf config.ai.localrun.enable pkgs.ollama)\n];","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/EE.nix","r":478,"sp":[10,22,5,7],"sh":"1c9e2d5dce64c6c7bd78a915784300bed243093e995a0f2a41cbce922c10ccba","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":481,"i":"5473f8e5-1013-4db6-a9ee-bc6d3299da41","k":"variable","n":"options","d":"options = {\n  engineer = {\n    enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable AI\";\n    localrun.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable local AI\";\n  };\n};","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/EE.nix","r":477,"sp":[3,8,3,5],"sh":"6fd45fcab6ec99557458dcd6d3cddfa22e3173fa0aec9faa9f4d83816e3ed8fc","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":482,"i":"41d52d86-ed3c-4f70-a3a7-43c7b65081f1","k":"module","n":"Desktop Application Configurations","d":"Collects and conditionally enables Home Manager configurations for a suite of desktop applications (e.g., librewolf, qutebrowser, foot, kitty, mpv, zathura, startpage). It sets up packages, program options, theming via the color scheme palette, MIME defaults, and integrates with system services like PipeWire, providing a centralized point for desktop app setup when the desktop environment is enabled.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/apps","r":468,"tg":["evidence:source","lang:nix","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":483,"i":"7bb4ab0d-4b5b-45c1-a68a-ed0b0ca59ac6","k":"file","n":"default.nix","d":"Home Manager desktop apps module that composes the default GUI package list and program enable flags under a desktop enable condition, and aggregates specific app sub-modules via imports.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/apps/default.nix","r":482,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":484,"i":"53cf99fe-13b4-48e6-9c30-a31debb6ac4d","k":"variable","n":"config","d":"config = lib.mkIf config.desktop.enable {\n  home.packages = with pkgs; [\n    brave\n    bitwarden-desktop\n    (lib.mkIf osConfig.services.pipewire.enable crosspipe)\n    (lib.mkIf osConfig.services.pipewire.pulse.enable pavucontrol)\n  ];\n  programs = {\n    librewolf.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n    qutebrowser.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n    foot.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n    kitty.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n    zathura.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n    mpv.enable = lib.mkIf config.media.enable (lib.mkDefault true);\n  };\n};","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/apps/default.nix","r":483,"sp":[11,26,3,5],"sh":"511e439f083d00bafef23057857e2eb72f2753b460d9c317a63eb2b5ebe1a1dc","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":485,"i":"a529894f-13fb-4e81-90d7-8154ca9ce40c","k":"variable","n":"home.packages","d":"home.packages = with pkgs; [\n  brave\n  bitwarden-desktop\n  (lib.mkIf osConfig.services.pipewire.enable crosspipe)\n  (lib.mkIf osConfig.services.pipewire.pulse.enable pavucontrol)\n];","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/apps/default.nix","r":484,"sp":[12,17,5,7],"sh":"5bcf3dd7df13535dc0fbfab671dbbf03ef3c824d73545f49b0895e5c6d60dbc4","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":486,"i":"f68c9c9f-51d2-463f-b4b3-3b5461d53396","k":"variable","n":"imports","d":"imports = [\n  ./firefox.nix\n  ./foot.nix\n  ./kitty.nix\n  ./mpv.nix\n  ./startpage.nix\n  ./zathura.nix\n];","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/apps/default.nix","r":483,"sp":[3,10,3,5],"sh":"3fa003004e352cf4ba131f93d33001558d72c27937c00b76b06560c6653fa8f4","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":487,"i":"3969b2eb-4953-46e7-a8e1-f65da29e791c","k":"variable","n":"programs","d":"programs = {\n  librewolf.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n  qutebrowser.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n  foot.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n  kitty.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n  zathura.enable = lib.mkDefault true;\n  mpv.enable = lib.mkIf config.media.enable (lib.mkDefault true);\n};","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/apps/default.nix","r":484,"sp":[18,25,5,7],"sh":"bf01996619ea725981a959d43b893c1d7fa1f940d706a718181867c88e5f57bf","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":488,"i":"387bbd33-f474-4299-b628-1aea95483a7f","k":"file","n":"firefox.nix","d":"Home-manager Firefox module that conditionally adds the nixffext helper script (for extracting extension IDs) when librewolf is enabled, and provides predefined locked option values for empty string, false, and true.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/apps/firefox.nix","r":482,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
