{"t":"n","a":650,"i":"292a6fe7-3330-4952-bbaa-6be764a5b58f","k":"file","n":"connect.py","d":"Copies a command into the Quickshell environment and sends it to the runner via the output channel, then awaits a response. It expects a string `cmd` to be passed, writes the UTF‑8 bytes of `cmd` to `self.output` followed by a newline, and blocks until `self.reader.receive()` returns the echo or response, which it then returns as a string. If the writer closes, it raises a `BrokenPipeError`; if the reader times out it raises a `TimeoutError`. The function is used by the REST handler to forward user‑sent commands to the shell process.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":596,"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":651,"i":"02a7ef84-3afb-4ce4-af8f-fb8464d9ca1a","k":"function","n":"connect_github","d":"Takes no arguments. Calls update_config to apply the GitHub integration configuration and returns whatever update_config returns (if any).","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":650,"sg":"def connect_github():","lt":"[\"Checking GitHub CLI authentication…\",\"gh\",\"auth\",\"status\",\"login\",\"GitHub login did not complete\",\"Repositories to monitor (owner/repo, comma separated): \",\"[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\"]","sp":[61,84,1,77],"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":652,"i":"0263931c-9e48-4eea-86a4-15fd4c9f6246","k":"function","n":"connect_proton","d":"Takes no arguments. Calls private_write and update_config to perform side‑effects, then returns None.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":650,"sg":"def connect_proton():","lt":"[\"Proton Bridge will open in CLI mode.\",\"Run `login`, then `info` to view the Bridge IMAP credentials, then `exit`.n\",\"protonmail-bridge\",\"--cli\",\"Proton Bridge setup did not complete\",\"Bridge IMAP username: \",\"Bridge-generated IMAP password: \",\"Both Bridge IMAP fields are required\"]","sp":[87,106,1,85],"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":653,"i":"7b75f5a6-f6d4-4b04-a644-91ebf2ba61fe","k":"function","n":"main","d":"Takes a list of command‑line arguments argv. Looks at the first argument to select a subcommand: if it is \"github\" it calls connect_github with the remaining arguments; if it is \"proton\" it calls connect_proton with the remaining arguments. Returns the value returned by the invoked subcommand. Raises ValueError if argv is empty or the subcommand name is not one of the supported ones. Propagates any exception raised by the called functions.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":650,"sg":"def main(argv):","lt":"[\"github\",\"proton\",\"Usage: connect.py github|proton\",\"systemctl\",\"--user\",\"restart\",\"graphide-shell.service\",\"nConnected. The company widgets are refreshing.\"]","sp":[109,119,1,13],"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":654,"i":"f959c347-f58d-41df-a70a-3b0c821cefc4","k":"function","n":"private_write","d":"Takes a filesystem path (string) and data (bytes or string) and writes the data to the file at the given path, overwriting any existing file. Returns None. Raises OSError if the file cannot be written.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":650,"sg":"def private_write(path, data):","lt":"[\".connect-\"]","sp":[35,48,1,33],"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":655,"i":"64856d77-8e4c-4dd4-9231-e51e1e484ce5","k":"function","n":"replace_section","d":"Takes a string `text` containing a TOML configuration, a string `name` identifying a section, and a mapping `values` of keys to values. Returns a string where the section named `name` in `text` is replaced by the TOML representation of `values` (produced via the `toml_value` helper). If the section does not exist, a new section with the given name and formatted values is appended to the end of the text. Raises a TypeError if `values` is not a mapping; raises a ValueError if `text` is not a string or `name` is empty.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":650,"sg":"def replace_section(text, name, values):","lt":"[\"]n\",\" = \",\"(?ms)^[\",\"][ t]*n.*?(?=^[|Z)\",\"nn\"]","sp":[25,32,1,71],"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":656,"i":"591639d5-c0ed-4b03-a63b-f941c4e63448","k":"function","n":"toml_value","d":"Takes a single argument `value` of any supported Python type and returns a string containing a TOML literal that represents the given value. Supported types are:\n- ``None`` → ``null``\n- ``bool`` → ``true`` or ``false``\n- ``int`` and ``float`` → the decimal representation without quoting\n- ``str`` → the string enclosed in double quotes, with interior double‑quote characters escaped as ``\\\"``\n- ``list`` or ``tuple`` → a bracketed list ``[ ... ]`` where each element is recursively encoded as a TOML literal and separated by commas; an empty sequence yields ``[]``\n- ``dict`` → an inline table ``{ key = value, ... }`` where keys are strings (unquoted if they match TOML bare identifiers, otherwise quoted) and values are recursively encoded; an empty mapping yields ``{}``\n- ``datetime.date``/``datetime.datetime``/``datetime.time`` → the ISO‑8601 representation enclosed in double quotes.\nFor any other type the function raises ``TypeError``. The returned string contains no trailing newline.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":650,"sg":"def toml_value(value):","lt":"[\"true\",\"false\"]","sp":[19,22,1,29],"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":657,"i":"6f5af6a8-c3b5-469c-860a-8b399140aa0c","k":"function","n":"update_config","d":"Takes a configuration section name (a string) and a mapping of values (a dict). Calls private_write with the given name and values to persist the new settings, then calls replace_section to update the corresponding section in the QuickShell configuration. Returns None on success, propagating any exception raised by the helper calls.","p":"modules/home-manager/desktop/env/wm/quickshell/shell/connect.py","r":650,"sg":"def update_config(name, values):","sp":[51,58,1,40],"tg":["description:agent","lang:python","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
