{"t":"n","a":1210,"i":"eb8b2965-f52c-4756-8c65-3b625273ae90","k":"file","n":"onTheGo.nix","d":"Defines the \"onTheGo\" NixOS specialisation, setting system tags, disabling Docker and Waydroid virtualization, and configuring the home-manager user profile for the portable environment.","p":"modules/nixos/onTheGo.nix","r":1079,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":1211,"i":"e1d6047f-2761-4cec-96b6-b6fadd775112","k":"variable","n":"onTheGo.configuration","d":"onTheGo.configuration = {\n      system.nixos.tags = [ \"onTheGo\" ];\n      virtualisation = {\n        docker.enable = false;\n        waydroid.enable = false;\n      };\n      home-manager = { \n        users.\"greencheetah\" = import ../home-manager/onTheGo.nix;\n      };\n      boot = {\n        extraModprobeConfig = ''\n          blacklist nouveau\n          options nouveau modeset=0\n          btusb\n          options iwlwifi power_save=1\n          options iwlwifi uapsd_disable=0\n          options iwlmvm power_scheme=3\n          '';\n… (truncated)","p":"modules/nixos/onTheGo.nix","r":1212,"sp":[4,57,5,7],"sh":"2aba12ed3978aec53d33dcbc0aa989cc54b825c6bc0417797ffe1a22c5b4aa5c","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1212,"i":"185145cc-741c-47b9-aaad-75e059363e6e","k":"variable","n":"specialisation","d":"specialisation = {\n    onTheGo.configuration = {\n      system.nixos.tags = [ \"onTheGo\" ];\n      virtualisation = {\n        docker.enable = false;\n        waydroid.enable = false;\n      };\n      home-manager = { \n        users.\"greencheetah\" = import ../home-manager/onTheGo.nix;\n      };\n      boot = {\n        extraModprobeConfig = ''\n          blacklist nouveau\n          options nouveau modeset=0\n          btusb\n          options iwlwifi power_save=1\n          options iwlwifi uapsd_disable=0\n          options iwlmvm power_scheme=3\n          '';\n… (truncated)","p":"modules/nixos/onTheGo.nix","r":1210,"sp":[3,58,3,5],"sh":"516ba143629b95fa16193631aa4c8a216d59d78e11642e48e0fbc8451b3a431e","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1213,"i":"14e7e287-79e9-446d-abeb-2ef9cc19d541","k":"module","n":"Home Server Service Suite","d":"Provides a collection of NixOS options and service definitions for personal server workloads, including a Matrix homeserver (continuwuity), Home Assistant, Mautrix bridges, media stack (Jellyfin, Sonarr, Radarr, etc.), Minecraft server, Nextcloud AIO, ntfy push server, WireGuard VPN, and email notification via you-have-mail. Each service can be enabled independently, with associated firewall rules, Caddy virtual hosts, and systemd units wired together.","p":"modules/nixos/serv","r":1214,"tg":["evidence:source","lang:nix","layer:architecture","source:arch-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":1214,"i":"af3c527c-0759-46f5-95e6-e4db6f65e1cf","k":"subsystem","n":"modules/nixos/serv — Server‑side system configuration","d":"Nix modules that configure server services, notably the Matrix service stack.","p":"modules/nixos/serv","r":1080,"tg":["evidence:signatures","layer:overview","overview:rung:directory","source:overview-agent"]}
{"t":"n","a":1215,"i":"2cf82213-fedf-4335-a787-7a4a742f4f9a","k":"file","n":"continuwuity.nix","d":"NixOS module file defining the `serv.continuwuity` option tree and, when enabled, configuring the upstream `services.matrix-continuwuity` homeserver, a Caddy virtual host terminating TLS for it, and the firewall ports it needs. Imported by `modules/nixos/serv/default.nix` alongside the Synapse-shaped `./matrix` module, which it deliberately does not touch.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1213,"tg":["lang:nix","plan:conduwuit-migration","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":1216,"i":"03a0b534-ca29-46c5-ba1d-047661b91c80","k":"module","n":"Continuwuity Matrix Homeserver Module","d":"Planning root for the conduwuit migration, retained as provenance now that `modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix` is built and extraction has adopted its symbols under the Server Services Module.\n\nThe module exposes `serv.continuwuity` on omegaServ, replacing the `girlbossceo/conduwuit:v0.4.7-rc` Docker container that ran on the host's previous Arch Linux install and adopting that container's RocksDB database from the `conduit_db` volume.\n\nDeliberately a sibling of, not a change to, `serv.matrix`: that module is Synapse-shaped, targets matrixServ, and keeps working untouched.\n\nIt wraps upstream `services.matrix-continuwuity` (0.5.10 — the conduwuit fork whose 0.5.x line continues conduwuit's 0.4.x numbering) with the retired container's settings: `server_name` chat.benmac.xyz, fixed forever by the existing database; `address` [ \"127.0.0.1\" ] and `port` [ 6167 ], where the container instead bound 0.0.0.0 and published 8008; `allow_registration` false; `allow_federation` true; `trusted_servers` [ \"matrix.org\" ]; `max_request_size` 50000000; and the `well_known` client and server URLs. The container's `CONDUIT_DATABASE_BACKEND=rocksdb` has no counterpart here — RocksDB is continuwuity's only backend and the option exists solely on the older `services.matrix-conduit` module.\n\nCaddy fronts it on 443 with TLS-ALPN-01, since port 80 is not forwarded to this host, proxying `/_matrix/*` and `/.well-known/matrix/*` to loopback. Only 443 is opened.\n\nMigrating the 1.4G database is deliberately not automated: upstream pins the path through systemd StateDirectory under DynamicUser, so it is a one-time operator step against a stopped service.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1214,"tg":["source:composite-make"]}
{"t":"n","a":1217,"i":"9931e8fb-a886-4743-9181-12a2a5ff645b","k":"variable","n":"acmeEmail","d":"acmeEmail = lib.mkOption {\n  type = lib.types.str;\n  description = \"Address ACME registers the certificate under.\";\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1225,"sp":[28,31,5,7],"sh":"bc7fea98b13a3e9830f57486cbbe32d9e4dfab680eb21668aea03172756e8bdf","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1218,"i":"1e341e46-6e95-471b-8b3f-b1c506d0ba72","k":"variable","n":"cfg","d":"cfg = config.serv.continuwuity;","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1215,"sp":[4,4,3,34],"sh":"c69ad5de813f3987d0603245ad251781a944668d2b908fe417dd9f05a61e353a","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1219,"i":"81a99e09-b56a-4143-a405-84e8fb87fa2e","k":"variable","n":"config","d":"The `lib.mkIf cfg.enable` block holding everything the module contributes: the homeserver service, its Caddy virtual host, and the firewall ports. Gated so that a host importing `modules/nixos/serv` without setting `serv.continuwuity.enable` gets none of it.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1215,"sp":[52,137,3,5],"sh":"7b180c7b4b89b9af22ec13f84f6bb474d03a0ceb289f70255dfd59ba03e8a83a","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:conduwuit-migration","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1220,"i":"1815ed28-e909-4db5-ab8c-fcacf0344588","k":"variable","n":"dataDir","d":"dataDir = lib.mkOption {\n  type = lib.types.nullOr lib.types.path;\n  default = null;\n  example = \"/home/continuwuity\";\n  description = ''\n    Directory the database is bind-mounted onto, for hosts whose root\n    filesystem is too small to hold it. Null leaves it in\n    /var/lib/continuwuity. Upstream pins `database_path` read-only to that\n    location, so a bind mount is the only way to relocate it.\n  '';\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1225,"sp":[39,49,5,7],"sh":"23777fc7496101b52617e9ed5dab3df078f8468ed1db667daf538a471167d3a6","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1221,"i":"6b6794ee-6639-4578-8025-262fc3e9e979","k":"variable","n":"enable","d":"enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"the continuwuity Matrix homeserver\";","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1225,"sp":[9,9,5,70],"sh":"cab27c8909c1b69f75b07d8fccda9ebc2132609c7d46278298b5f024c26909ec","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1222,"i":"af085887-7433-4a3c-969e-9d19c1a77a90","k":"variable","n":"hostname","d":"hostname = lib.mkOption {\n  type = lib.types.str;\n  default = cfg.serverName;\n  defaultText = lib.literalExpression \"config.serv.continuwuity.serverName\";\n  description = \"Public FQDN Caddy obtains a certificate for.\";\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1225,"sp":[21,26,5,7],"sh":"be982f6b3111dfcd36d7cf8955423a877a6d6e7cebfb27ce81937e0b2ab595b5","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1223,"i":"a6f73225-37a1-4dbd-8039-821bcd25cfd2","k":"variable","n":"listenAddress","d":"listenAddress = \"127.0.0.1:${toString cfg.port}\";","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1215,"sp":[5,5,3,52],"sh":"d5155e4e0650ee44dfab08f4998f9a93d147199389e598aa07997511feae9ce7","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1224,"i":"c68a624e-8246-4607-8a73-c43a7aca17aa","k":"variable","n":"networking.firewall.allowedTCPPorts","d":"Opens 443 only, matching what `serv/ntfy.nix` does on this host. Port 80 is deliberately left closed: it is not forwarded to this machine, which is why the Caddy vhost disables the HTTP-01 challenge. cfg.port is not opened either — the old container published the homeserver directly as host port 8008, and moving it behind Caddy on loopback is the change this migration makes.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1219,"lt":"[\"443\"]","sp":[109,109,5,51],"sh":"a41c61a3998d43b8254c284a80847bf19502ef1be68d2d23d51f10c14372ee98","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","nix:leaf","plan:conduwuit-migration","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1225,"i":"d117dc18-bcad-4bb8-b4a9-40bf0d157197","k":"variable","n":"options.serv.continuwuity","d":"The module's option tree. `enable` is an mkEnableOption. `serverName` (str) is the Matrix domain baked into every user and room id in the adopted database — it defaults to \"chat.benmac.xyz\" and must never change, because the existing RocksDB was written under it. `hostname` (str, default `serverName`) is the public FQDN Caddy obtains a certificate for. `acmeEmail` (str) is the ACME registration address. `port` (port, default 6167) is the loopback port the homeserver listens on, matching the retired container's CONDUIT_PORT.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1215,"sp":[8,50,3,5],"sh":"3cfc0c5e2604f80761b78dbd3a2d9d02408f2ae6a7cba5e7b6fa57f8036b4f40","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","nix:option","plan:conduwuit-migration","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1226,"i":"95b419f1-2cb0-4e0b-9289-250ac99984c6","k":"variable","n":"port","d":"port = lib.mkOption {\n  type = lib.types.port;\n  default = 6167;\n  description = ''\n    Loopback port the homeserver listens on. Matches the CONDUIT_PORT of\n    the container this replaces; only Caddy reaches it.\n  '';\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1225,"sp":[33,37,5,7],"sh":"e7551c6b6fb64665f29416c5c00f0ee0fdac1964bbc106e92179836caf91677e","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1227,"i":"4f7d63a0-51a2-48d9-870a-1a33029cbab9","k":"variable","n":"serverName","d":"serverName = lib.mkOption {\n  type = lib.types.str;\n  default = \"chat.benmac.xyz\";\n  description = ''\n    The Matrix domain. Every user and room id in the database carries it as\n    a suffix, so it cannot be changed after the first start without\n    orphaning all of them. The default is the name the adopted database was\n    written under.\n  '';\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1225,"sp":[11,19,5,7],"sh":"5cd9551f3c490c29c023a67510eff6b30a01602114b5be0d626a4fd87bb0ef32","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1228,"i":"5fc3a232-63ea-49af-b86c-937e4b32fa5d","k":"variable","n":"services.caddy","d":"Terminates TLS for the homeserver, following the pattern `serv/ntfy.nix` established on this host. Enables Caddy with `email = lib.mkDefault cfg.acmeEmail` — mkDefault so that enabling this module alongside `serv.ntfy`, which sets the same option outright, does not collide. The virtual host for cfg.hostname forces the ACME TLS-ALPN-01 challenge via `disable_http_challenge`, because port 80 is not forwarded to this host; sets the same three security headers the ntfy vhost does; and reverse-proxies both `/_matrix/*` (with the request body limit raised to 50MB to match max_request_size) and `/.well-known/matrix/*` to 127.0.0.1:${cfg.port}. Discovery is proxied rather than served as inline JSON so that the `well_known` settings in the homeserver config remain the single source of truth.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1219,"lt":"[\"/_matrix/*\",\"/.well-known/matrix/*\",\"disable_http_challenge\"]","sp":[73,107,5,7],"sh":"501748ee12ea1fdba0f84771f382dea144f3d9e1fdd07faeab3df7df006a1fb7","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:conduwuit-migration","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1229,"i":"e8735864-e120-47ee-aea5-ef98fba70930","k":"variable","n":"services.matrix-continuwuity","d":"Enables the upstream continuwuity homeserver with the settings carried over from the retired `girlbossceo/conduwuit:v0.4.7-rc` container, so the adopted RocksDB is opened as it was written. Sets `settings.global`: `server_name` from cfg.serverName; `address` [ \"127.0.0.1\" ] and `port` [ cfg.port ] (the container bound 0.0.0.0 and published 8008; Caddy now sits in front on the same host); `allow_registration` false; `allow_federation` true; `trusted_servers` [ \"matrix.org\" ]; `max_request_size` 50000000; and `well_known.client` / `well_known.server`, which the freeform submodule passes through to TOML. Omits the container's `CONDUIT_DATABASE_BACKEND=rocksdb`: that option exists only on the older `services.matrix-conduit` module, because RocksDB is continuwuity's sole backend. Leaves `database_path` alone — upstream pins it to /var/lib/continuwuity through systemd StateDirectory and asserts against any other value.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1219,"lt":"[\"127.0.0.1\",\"matrix.org\"]","sp":[53,71,5,7],"sh":"78a971d39d9d42bf8532e9578f9a2f2550bf24a3e113f4fee72473800166e3db","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:conduwuit-migration","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1230,"i":"57df0dde-245c-4d99-bf72-748f82f2478d","k":"variable","n":"systemd.mounts","d":"Bind-mounts the homeserver's state directory onto cfg.dataDir, so the Matrix database lives on the host's 8TB /home spindle instead of its 128GB root SSD. Emitted only when cfg.dataDir is non-null.\n\nA bind mount is the only lever available: upstream declares `settings.global.database_path` as `readOnly = true`, pinned to /var/lib/continuwuity, because the service relies on systemd StateDirectory. The mount point is `/var/lib/private/continuwuity` rather than /var/lib/continuwuity, because `DynamicUser = true` makes the latter a symlink into the former.\n\n**This is `systemd.mounts` and not a `fileSystems` entry, and the distinction is why the host stayed reachable.** A `fileSystems` entry is boot-critical: if it fails, `local-fs.target` fails and the machine drops to emergency mode with no sshd. It did fail, because `/var/lib/private` does not exist until a DynamicUser service has run at least once, so nothing had created the mount point on a fresh boot. As a plain mount unit, pulled in by `RequiresMountsFor` on continuwuity.service, a failure now confines itself to that one service.\n\nPaired with tmpfiles rules creating cfg.dataDir, /var/lib/private and the mount point itself, and with `unitConfig.RequiresMountsFor = cfg.dataDir` so the mount orders after whatever filesystem holds the target.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1219,"lt":"[\"/var/lib/private/continuwuity\",\"bind\"]","sp":[120,132,1,7],"sh":"daee09243a6c402987c156918f63757a8588b4bb57b58b23d929c370f0cd63f6","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:conduwuit-migration","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1231,"i":"40031468-8e78-43cd-87cc-14fb549a62e2","k":"variable","n":"systemd.services.continuwuity.unitConfig","d":"systemd.services.continuwuity.unitConfig = lib.mkIf (cfg.dataDir != null) {\n  RequiresMountsFor = \"/var/lib/private/continuwuity\";\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1219,"sp":[134,136,5,7],"sh":"f25efbee620d4cfc179621cc3aaf86a2ce8355a34b4a9a6883e276e9f562ab2f","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1232,"i":"9bf0ca48-e4b8-4ab9-aeba-7a10f63ba292","k":"variable","n":"systemd.tmpfiles.rules","d":"systemd.tmpfiles.rules = lib.mkIf (cfg.dataDir != null) [\n  \"d ${cfg.dataDir} 0700 root root -\"\n];","p":"modules/nixos/serv/continuwuity.nix","r":1219,"sp":[111,118,1,7],"sh":"e1ec2ebc3ac2f7386fd21b74c8c4333f3864e921f8efd8dc7886880513f27a0d","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1233,"i":"0aea0eb2-1bd0-4a39-9a64-69f7b46ae190","k":"file","n":"default.nix","d":"NixOS serv module that, when enabled, configures OpenSSH with secure defaults and imports the home-assistant, matrix, media, minecraft, and wireguard service sub-modules, exposing a serv.enable option.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/default.nix","r":1213,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":1234,"i":"a5910e59-0d4c-4d1a-b702-1125b64a102f","k":"variable","n":"config","d":"config = lib.mkIf config.serv.enable\n{\n  services.openssh = {\n    enable = true;\n    settings = {\n      PasswordAuthentication = lib.mkDefault false;\n      UseDns = true;\n      PermitRootLogin = \"no\"; # \"yes\", \"without-password\", \"prohibit-password\", \"forced-commands-only\", \"no\"\n    };\n  };\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/default.nix","r":1233,"sp":[20,30,3,7],"sh":"d9b35b9a778e35242abdc58ac142e0635ad23d41d35d33b290a8475384a13923","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1235,"i":"b56a7295-a8e9-420c-9492-3f2e27bc5373","k":"variable","n":"imports","d":"imports = [\n  ./home-assistant.nix\n  ./matrix\n  ./media.nix\n  ./minecraft.nix\n  ./wireguard.nix\n];","p":"modules/nixos/serv/default.nix","r":1233,"sp":[7,18,3,5],"sh":"07b94a7de3f0fe968f68241ebf5a7b22faf810950afc8c83710148eb4b757a11","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1236,"i":"3cbb9002-8b69-4341-8109-704caa0af1d1","k":"variable","n":"options.serv.enable","d":"options.serv.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable the serv module\";","p":"modules/nixos/serv/default.nix","r":1233,"sp":[19,19,3,69],"sh":"d0e503674c81142f876aaa715388b12cdcb1a1fba7191abb74b28718b774f931","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","nix:option","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1237,"i":"cca6c060-8125-4e5a-9e46-f85aa89605d9","k":"variable","n":"services.openssh","d":"services.openssh = {\n  enable = true;\n  settings = {\n    PasswordAuthentication = lib.mkDefault false;\n    UseDns = true;\n    PermitRootLogin = \"no\"; # \"yes\", \"without-password\", \"prohibit-password\", \"forced-commands-only\", \"no\"\n  };\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/default.nix","r":1234,"sp":[22,29,7,9],"sh":"6745d102c933297356608878408176bd46a83d089ec713d4db53934a4e66aaf1","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1238,"i":"6fb436eb-0a76-4938-a75a-fa3832ccf178","k":"variable","n":"upkgs","d":"upkgs = pkgs.unstable;","p":"modules/nixos/serv/default.nix","r":1233,"sp":[4,4,3,25],"sh":"e27ed9700548bf0fc029dfc025310a7f826a0ce93f485168d95dc58752bf8777","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1239,"i":"28270805-0fdf-42ca-a669-04394440cc1f","k":"file","n":"home-assistant.nix","d":"NixOS module configuring the Home Assistant service, adding default and extra components and automatically opening port 8123 in the firewall when enabled.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/home-assistant.nix","r":1213,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
