{"t":"n","a":1323,"i":"6241555e-5d47-4b6a-b309-c7d9921424db","k":"variable","n":"services.caddy","d":"services.caddy = {\n  enable = true;\n  email = cfg.acmeEmail;\n\n  virtualHosts.${cfg.hostName}.extraConfig = ''\n    encode zstd gzip\n\n    header {\n      Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\"\n      X-Content-Type-Options \"nosniff\"\n      Referrer-Policy \"same-origin\"\n    }\n\n    handle /_matrix/* {\n      request_body {\n        max_size 100MB\n      }\n      reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8008\n    }\n\n    handle /_synapse/client/* {\n      reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8008\n    }\n\n    handle /.well-known/matrix/server {\n      header Content-Type application/json\n… (truncated)","p":"modules/nixos/serv/matrix/web.nix","r":1320,"sp":[34,76,5,7],"sh":"48e6fd89e518bde050d2b9655d28cd6351883b20f071782d3467e76bb8b4631b","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1324,"i":"7e48b038-667d-4cd8-80d3-e0d62f1c3f0a","k":"variable","n":"wellKnownClient","d":"wellKnownClient = builtins.toJSON {\n  \"m.homeserver\".base_url = \"https://${cfg.hostName}\";\n  \"org.matrix.msc3575.proxy\".url = \"https://${cfg.hostName}\";\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/matrix/web.nix","r":1314,"sp":[11,14,3,5],"sh":"e9bf56d40bd5647f859943a161ea3466afa25b13250c71b78f582dd5c63f060e","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1325,"i":"13a9a9fc-ee43-43e9-bedb-86b1a35df991","k":"variable","n":"wellKnownServer","d":"wellKnownServer = builtins.toJSON { \"m.server\" = \"${cfg.hostName}:443\"; };","p":"modules/nixos/serv/matrix/web.nix","r":1314,"sp":[10,10,3,77],"sh":"afc1aa4e7e4258de749dbf55b870f1c53439cd0a7a201cc1f7b513775cb5dfa9","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1326,"i":"7a33c5d4-0396-44c5-82bf-6b98f069bc13","k":"file","n":"mautrix-bridges.nix","d":"NixOS module file defining the `serv.mautrixBridges` option tree and, when enabled, configuring the upstream mautrix-whatsapp and mautrix-discord services against the local continuwuity homeserver, plus the PostgreSQL databases they store bridge state in. Imported by `modules/nixos/serv/default.nix`.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1213,"tg":["lang:nix","plan:mautrix-bridges","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":1327,"i":"d087ca82-fab4-478d-b18e-d1b6abee998f","k":"function","n":"socketUri","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1326,"sg":"socketUri = db:","lt":"[\"postgres:///${db}?host=/run/postgresql\"]","sp":[7,7,3,60],"tg":["arch:auto-attached","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1328,"i":"338dd36d-615d-4037-ab3b-a7677193ea03","k":"variable","n":"assertions","d":"assertions = [\n  {\n    assertion = matrix.enable;\n    message = \"serv.mautrixBridges requires serv.continuwuity.enable; the bridges have no other homeserver to register against.\";\n  }\n];","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1330,"sp":[27,32,5,7],"sh":"b4522453f3d689ec9d67c7e2e854e983265c845f9c05dfe7f3513b435dba4e9d","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1329,"i":"21becee1-f808-40fc-89dc-2b135ae966f1","k":"variable","n":"cfg","d":"cfg = config.serv.mautrixBridges;","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1326,"sp":[4,4,3,36],"sh":"fc8b565c705bcec875177b36b859be69011afcf6b6c67df3fe70408647a70cc2","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1330,"i":"0a9e6508-e318-437d-81ae-816153d39e65","k":"variable","n":"config","d":"The `lib.mkIf cfg.enable` block holding the two bridge service configurations and the PostgreSQL databases behind them.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1326,"sp":[26,116,3,5],"sh":"f1a5b046b7daaafc738bc2b942041dca98be93ec2c33950df9da4d75f4f05abe","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:mautrix-bridges","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1331,"i":"fb4352a4-ec45-4c49-b87d-3e3c8d089242","k":"variable","n":"discord.enable","d":"discord.enable = lib.mkOption {\n  type = lib.types.bool;\n  default = true;\n  description = \"Run the Discord bridge.\";\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1335,"sp":[19,23,5,7],"sh":"08ca0a4cdebc32e381e7658f18fe2943778095cfe5721fb5b003b9b8efea8890","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1332,"i":"a3f4736d-2c28-488e-8350-3d714c66c52d","k":"variable","n":"enable","d":"enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"the mautrix puppeting bridges\";","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1335,"sp":[11,11,5,65],"sh":"1d7b99fbf9d25c91d2115c334fc6fccd14adcfaae2b2bc5c765a7ba7b825b024","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1333,"i":"bac46b7e-6316-4eea-8cc6-68d2fdc7b4ea","k":"variable","n":"homeserverAddress","d":"homeserverAddress = \"http://127.0.0.1:${toString matrix.port}\";","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1326,"sp":[6,6,3,66],"sh":"353abf5c00cef3687644d9ca3ca90bc530487ab09d6fcbcd480abf55abda4900","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1334,"i":"50e4455f-0be2-410d-bf25-9862b98ab9f7","k":"variable","n":"matrix","d":"matrix = config.serv.continuwuity;","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1326,"sp":[5,5,3,37],"sh":"dd6ae23a49d658a2b08d5bea5781d6e3eeb4d701de2bb9f1d279a19ae0647008","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1335,"i":"2f0dfbfb-d11c-4ab7-8b97-a1b57df3ae62","k":"variable","n":"options.serv.mautrixBridges","d":"The module's option tree: `enable` gates the whole thing, and `whatsapp.enable` / `discord.enable` select individual bridges, both defaulting to true so that enabling the module brings up the pair that was running before. Slack has no option — it was explicitly dropped from scope. Everything else the bridges need is read from `config.serv.continuwuity`, so there is no domain or homeserver address to restate here and no way for the two to drift apart.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1326,"sp":[10,24,3,5],"sh":"af0313a73e8136fc5de53d6400e849c3c7ca62b9555236af58f968ac8a3807c7","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","nix:option","plan:mautrix-bridges","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1336,"i":"11a7551a-d397-4558-b343-1cec8efbc00f","k":"variable","n":"services.mautrix-discord","d":"Runs the Discord puppeting bridge when cfg.discord.enable, against the same homeserver as its WhatsApp sibling.\n\nUnlike WhatsApp's, this module's `settings.homeserver` and `settings.appservice` are `lib.types.attrs`, where a definition replaces the upstream default outright instead of merging into it. Both are therefore restated in full — including keys this module does not care about, like `software`, `ping_interval_seconds` and the bot avatar — because omitting any of them would drop it from the generated config rather than inherit it.\n\nThe restated identity matches the retired container: id \"discord\", bot username \"discordbot\", port 29334, with hostname narrowed from 0.0.0.0 to 127.0.0.1. The `as_token` and `hs_token` placeholders are upstream's own; the systemd preStart overwrites them from the generated registration file.\n\n`appservice.database` is postgres over the unix socket — note the nesting, which differs from WhatsApp's top-level `database`.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1330,"lt":"[\"discord\",\"discordbot\",\"127.0.0.1\",\"postgres\"]","sp":[54,97,5,7],"sh":"a94e007e1c8631d5e538ba00247eb9a88d0a457dacb4ff899408b3129a8ef8d0","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:mautrix-bridges","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1337,"i":"8662b18d-bbc9-42b9-bc4f-cde28ba745b2","k":"variable","n":"services.mautrix-whatsapp","d":"Runs the WhatsApp puppeting bridge when cfg.whatsapp.enable. Sets `settings.homeserver.domain` to the continuwuity serverName and `settings.homeserver.address` to its loopback URL, because upstream only auto-derives those for matrix-synapse and matrix-conduit and would otherwise leave its default http://localhost:8448.\n\nPartial settings are safe here: the option carries `apply = lib.recursiveUpdate defaultConfig`, so anything unset falls back to upstream deeply. The appservice identity is therefore not restated — upstream already defaults to id \"whatsapp\", bot username \"whatsappbot\", username_template \"whatsapp_{{.}}\" and port 29318, which are exactly what the retired container used, so the existing bot user and portal rooms are adopted rather than duplicated. Only `appservice.hostname` is overridden, from \"[::]\" to 127.0.0.1.\n\n`settings.database` is postgres over the unix socket, replacing the upstream sqlite3-fk-wal default, so the WhatsApp pairing surviving in the old container's database can be restored rather than re-done from the phone.\n\n`serviceDependencies` gains continuwuity.service and postgresql.service.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1330,"lt":"[\"whatsapp\",\"whatsappbot\",\"127.0.0.1\",\"postgres\"]","sp":[34,52,5,7],"sh":"70553cbeb87423e836ad99d37d8612c7db74f3f35368ef8b0009caf6b28e98f0","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:mautrix-bridges","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1338,"i":"d0a457f7-6cc8-4770-8250-e4b67402d17b","k":"variable","n":"services.postgresql","d":"Provides the bridge databases. Enables PostgreSQL and, for each enabled bridge, ensures a database named after it owned by a role of the same name, matching the system user the upstream module runs the bridge as.\n\nPeer authentication over the unix socket is what makes this passwordless: the old deployment put credentials in a connection URI in the bridge config, which is how its password ended up leaking during this migration. Nothing here writes a secret to the Nix store.\n\nThe database names deliberately do not match the old container's, which used a shared role \"funnylemon\" across databases named \"database\", \"discord\" and \"slack\". Restoring the old dumps into these differently-named databases is an operator step.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1330,"lt":"[\"mautrix-whatsapp\",\"mautrix-discord\"]","sp":[99,115,5,7],"sh":"13fceb1dc5293fa4f6b543c7e4ebb2382edbcfd1f0af76d612e5912c9fda945b","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","plan:mautrix-bridges","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1339,"i":"6cf2e659-344d-470e-8daf-51c329815536","k":"variable","n":"whatsapp.enable","d":"whatsapp.enable = lib.mkOption {\n  type = lib.types.bool;\n  default = true;\n  description = \"Run the WhatsApp bridge.\";\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/mautrix-bridges.nix","r":1335,"sp":[13,17,5,7],"sh":"5a806d51133a05456a2eac5cb946dafdb8fbe210df0a8e6c4df46d16395cde83","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1340,"i":"5a716b0a-4ce5-4b0c-a258-86240535b50b","k":"file","n":"media.nix","d":"Provides a NixOS module for the media service suite: defines a enable option and, when enabled, creates a media group with service users, configures the Jellyfin service (open firewall, data directory), and ensures the /srv/media directory exists with appropriate permissions.","p":"modules/nixos/serv/media.nix","r":1213,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":1341,"i":"7094dcf5-8400-4cc3-bd27-3d656edf144e","k":"variable","n":"config","d":"config = lib.mkIf config.serv.media.enable\n{\n  users.groups.media.members = [ \"prowlarr\" \"radarr\" \"sonarr\" \"readarr\" \"deluge\" \"jellyfin\" ];\n  services.jellyfin = {\n    openFirewall = true;\n    enable = true;\n    dataDir = \"/srv/media\";\n  };\n  systemd.tmpfiles.rules = [\n    \"d /srv/media 0775 jellyfin media\"\n    \"d /srv/media/movies 0775 jellyfin media\"\n    \"d /srv/media/tv 0775 jellyfin media\"\n    \"d /srv/media/anime 0775 jellyfin media\"\n    \"d /srv/media/music 0775 jellyfin media\"\n    \"d /srv/media/books 0775 jellyfin media\"\n    \"d /srv/media/downloads 0775 jellyfin media\"\n… (truncated)","p":"modules/nixos/serv/media.nix","r":1340,"sp":[4,45,3,7],"sh":"8b94a3ff0610f3c80c023c5c9a475475cb8a39446427af7d4c5158ca1043e03a","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1342,"i":"b481c1c7-9542-479e-a1a4-9118e88d5ed4","k":"variable","n":"options.serv.media.enable","d":"options.serv.media.enable = lib.mkEnableOption \"Enable media\";","p":"modules/nixos/serv/media.nix","r":1340,"sp":[3,3,3,65],"sh":"e2ea19821b1e42c1f71e6cedaa9bb7641aac6d5e35dfced0097ea72479978552","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","nix:option","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1343,"i":"3b5d1518-09de-4b63-b0cf-c7d5559edbd3","k":"variable","n":"services.deluge","d":"services.deluge = {\n  enable = true;\n  web = {\n    enable = true;\n    openFirewall = true;\n  };\n};","p":"modules/nixos/serv/media.nix","r":1341,"sp":[37,43,7,9],"sh":"264394683a189bb1c29caf8fac0e1ac96b9800ea46e5a04551a2ffae190bccc2","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
