{"t":"n","a":1427,"i":"9be847c1-2eec-4248-95c1-5d964fccebf8","k":"file","n":"tailscale.nix","d":"NixOS module that introduces the custom.tailscale.enable option and, when enabled, runs the Tailscale client daemon: services.tailscale with openFirewall (UDP 41641 for direct peer connections) and useRoutingFeatures = \"none\", plus networking.firewall.trustedInterfaces = [ \"tailscale0\" ] so tailnet peers bypass the host's port lists. Deliberately carries no auth key — the machine is logged in once out of band with `sudo tailscale up`, and node state persists in /var/lib/tailscale.","p":"modules/nixos/tailscale.nix","r":1079,"tg":["lang:nix","source:tree-sitter"]}
{"t":"n","a":1428,"i":"ec736bf9-c0f8-4811-af26-af63d9d69c66","k":"variable","n":"config","d":"config = lib.mkIf config.custom.tailscale.enable {\n  services.tailscale = {\n    enable = true;\n    openFirewall = true;\n    useRoutingFeatures = \"none\";\n  };\n\n  networking.firewall.trustedInterfaces = [ config.services.tailscale.interfaceName ];\n};","p":"modules/nixos/tailscale.nix","r":1427,"sp":[41,52,3,5],"sh":"733ab3e63ef60923b96d63e9a6faaacd534c0fbb067eb0d4f80a73d5e21388f0","tg":["arch:auto-attached","description:declaration","lang:nix","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
{"t":"n","a":1429,"i":"8ca06934-692c-4f93-b344-3ddd04d38bda","k":"variable","n":"networking.firewall.trustedInterfaces","d":"networking.firewall.trustedInterfaces = [ config.services.tailscale.interfaceName ];","p":"modules/nixos/tailscale.nix","r":1428,"sp":[48,48,5,89],"sh":"c1abd4a9d9328f888e9df30aeb3f29605c2723cba074d3086353f62fc68d3ffd","tg":["description:declaration","lang:nix","nix:leaf","source:tree-sitter","visibility:public"]}
